[a8w4_compact] 0001 - AIV stage: bulk-load group_list into UB before walking it.

Why
---
GMMA8W4PostProcess::UpdateVecConfig runs on every AIV core (40 of them) and
walks the full expert range twice with groupListGM.GetValue(i), i.e. blocking
scalar GM reads per expert per core.  At T=24 with E=256 the AIV stage costs
28.4 us against 6.95 us with E=8; the whole delta is this walk and it vanishes
once the list is read from UB.  Same values, same order, same arithmetic, so
numerics are bit-identical.

The AIC side is NOT fixed here: the cube core has no UB, so the same trick is
unavailable to GMMA8W4MidProcess (63.6 us of aic_scalar).  That half needs a
compacted active-expert table produced on the AIV - see ../README.md, phase 2.

Applies to:
  op_impl/ai_core/tbe/custom_transformer_impl/ascendc/grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2/
    grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2_a8w4_msd_post.h

